t/03-integration.t line 38 asserts _build_request('GET','/repos/my%20org/my%20repo') double-encodes to /repos/my%2520org/my%2520repo. But WWW::Forgejo OWNS the path-encoding semantics, and its t/05-urlencode.t codifies the opposite contract: controllers uri_escape their variable segments and _build_request passes the assembled path through VERBATIM (only query params are encoded). The sibling's line-35 assertion (/repos/owner/my-repo unchanged) already matches that contract; line 38 does not. Making _build_request escape % in the path to satisfy line 38 would break WWW::Forgejo t/05 (a controller-encoded %20 becomes %2520 and its qr/%20/ assertion fails), so the shared seam must NOT change -- the fix belongs in THIS test. Update the line-38 assertion to expect the path passed through verbatim (/repos/my%20org/my%20repo) and drop the 'double-encoded' wording. Verified 2026-09-18: with WWW::Forgejo phase2 landed on main, the full sibling offline suite is green EXCEPT this single assertion. Baseline blocker 2 of WWW-Forgejo#10; blockers 1 (url accessor) and 3 (/api/v1) are resolved on the WWW::Forgejo side.

